{"parentUuid":"855ff737-b650-462a-b7e3-3fcc0ff22c90","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mVXNnmt9mTnw6eYMTkYu6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT logical_objective best_objective_bound serialize protobuf checkpoint multi-run 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Using the CP-SAT solver - ortools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Rostering: Complete Guide to Constraint Programming for Workforce Scheduling - Interactive | Michael Brenndoerfer | Michael Brenndoerfer\",\"url\":\"https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/cp-sat-rostering-constraint-programming-workforce-scheduling\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Debugging the model\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/x84toCnIWnU/m/nyF4cJ-XAwAJ\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/model.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/model.md\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found related to CP-SAT and the various technical terms in your query:\n\n## CP-SAT Overview\n\nThe CP-SAT solver uses the cp_model protobuf, and calling the Solve() method returns a CpSolverResponse protobuf that contains the solve status, variable values, and metrics.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n**best_objective_bound**: A feasible solution has been found, and a bound may be available to assess its quality via solver.best_objective_bound.\n\n**Protobuf & Serialization**: The model can be exported using export_to_file() which auto-detects format by extension. The model is read from its protobuf representation.\n\n**logical_objective**: The search results mention logical constraints and objectives in CP-SAT, where CP-SAT provides an extensive set of constraints closer to high-level modeling languages like MiniZinc than to traditional Mixed Integer Programming, offering constraints like all_different and add_multiplication_equality.\n\n**Multi-run/Checkpoint**: CP-SAT concurrently executes diverse algorithms and strategies that operate largely independently but engage in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific 2025 updates or detailed documentation about these exact parameter combinations together, but they provide foundational information about how these concepts work in CP-SAT.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0b590c2f-a175-4130-b293-acf23d6e8bfb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:53.016Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"855ff737-b650-462a-b7e3-3fcc0ff22c90","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9