{"parentUuid":"e128a9a5-40ee-4a50-9e1f-7e1c37508e00","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpjZiRijd9a7hadrAK1nKt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Benders decomposition cut sharing multi-instance bound transfer LBBD 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Multicut logic‐based Benders decomposition for discrete‐time scheduling and dynamic optimization of network batch plants - Liñán - 2024 - AIChE Journal - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://aiche.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/aic.18491\"},{\"title\":\"Enhanced logic-based Benders decomposition methods for the distributed heterogeneous non-permutation flow shop scheduling problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 63 , No 24 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2025.2553820?mi=ik0enr\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/combinatorial-benders-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"Stochastic Planning and Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2022.1184\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders Decomposition and Binary Decision Diagram Based Approaches for Stochastic Distributed Operating Room Scheduling – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2019/07/7320/\"},{\"title\":\"Risk-aware Logic-based Benders Decomposition for a ...\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/SLAP-2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-based Benders decomposition for planning and scheduling: a computational analysis | The Knowledge Engineering Review | Cambridge Core\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/knowledge-engineering-review/article/abs/logicbased-benders-decomposition-for-planning-and-scheduling-a-computational-analysis/70EE77BFAE516C56F3363A90A3786D84\"},{\"title\":\"A logic-based benders decomposition method for refrigerated container stacking and relocation problem: International Journal of Production Research: Vol 0, No 0 - Get Access\",\"url\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/00207543.2025.2598024\"},{\"title\":\"Solving logic-based benders decomposition master problems with constraint programming and domain-independent dynamic programming | Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10601-025-09382-1\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition for Unmanned Electric Tugboat Scheduling Considering Battery-Swapping Operations\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2077-1312/13/9/1633\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on \"Benders decomposition cut sharing multi-instance bound transfer LBBD 2024 2025\". Here's a summary of the relevant findings:\n\n## Recent LBBD Research (2024-2025)\n\nThe search results reveal several recent developments in Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (LBBD):\n\n### Key Applications and Enhancements\n\nA 2024 study presents the first application of logic-based Benders decomposition in simultaneous scheduling and dynamic optimization of network batch processes, employing neighborhood information of ordered discrete decisions to generate cuts rather than traditional dual information techniques.\n\nEnhanced LBBD methods for flow shop scheduling integrate advanced techniques such as strong subproblem relaxations, tightened lower bounds, and constraint programming.\n\n### Cut Generation and Management\n\nIn hybrid control policies for robotic systems, feasibility and optimality Benders cuts derived via dual solutions from subproblems are stored in online buffers and re-used across successive iterations, enabling rapid warm-starting and outperforming commercial solvers.\n\nDynamic approaches include selective separation, adaptive cut management, and dynamic aggregation to increase tractability for large problem instances.\n\n### Recent Algorithm Development\n\nRecent research investigates using Constraint Programming and Domain-Independent Dynamic Programming to solve LBBD master problems, exploiting variable assignment bounds and global constraints to construct combinatorial cut encodings.\n\nA 2025 study on refrigerated container logistics applies LBBD with several master problem strengthening strategies to obtain tighter lower bounds.\n\nThe results show that LBBD continues to be an active research area with focus on cut sharing mechanisms, bound improvements, and multi-instance optimization strategies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e4dfd437-2194-445d-a4ff-446c82b35e2a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:54.460Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e128a9a5-40ee-4a50-9e1f-7e1c37508e00","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3ce77d1b-f0fa-42fb-8c78-3caec27ab2c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CtxeGqde8ED9epdwLGq5GG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"dual ray\" serialize farkas certificate infeasibility Gurobi CPLEX 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Get the extreme ray from infeasible primal – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/15448804407697-Get-the-extreme-ray-from-infeasible-primal\"},{\"title\":\"Farkas certificate – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360055293151-Farkas-certificate\"},{\"title\":\"Get infeasibility certificate in CPLEX or Gurobi - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/get-infeasibility-certificate-in-cplex-or-gurobi/50506\"},{\"title\":\"FarkasDual and FarkasProof – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360078072572-FarkasDual-and-FarkasProof\"},{\"title\":\"zero dual variables\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/gurobi/c/UWoyXBMyVBI\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Farkas Certificates in CPLEX\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2011/07/farkas-certificates-in-cplex.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Infeasible LPs and Farkas Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2010/07/infeasible-lps-and-farkas-certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"Does FarkasDual of an infeasible primal lp return the unbounded ray of its dual?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/d/topic/gurobi/TNLfMtQXVzQ\"},{\"title\":\"Get infeasibility certificate in CPLEX or Gurobi - #3 by odow - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/get-infeasibility-certificate-in-cplex-or-gurobi/50506/3\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Guidelines - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/concepts/parameters/guidelines.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about dual ray, Farkas certificates, and infeasibility in Gurobi and CPLEX:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Farkas Certificates and Infeasibility:**\nA Farkas certificate is a vector of constraint multipliers that proves a primal linear program to be infeasible, named after Farkas's Lemma.\n\n**Retrieving Infeasibility Proofs in Gurobi:**\nWhen you set the InfUnbdInfo parameter for an infeasible model, you can retrieve a Farkas infeasibility proof using the FarkasDual and FarkasProof attributes.\n\n**Relationship to Dual Rays:**\nGurobi's FarkasDual provides a dual unbounded vector, offering a Farkas infeasibility proof for infeasible linear models. In linear Benders decomposition, you need the dual ray (Farkas certificate) for feasibility cuts rather than dual variables.\n\n**Variable Bounds Consideration:**\nIf your model has nontrivial upper and/or lower bounds on variables, you may need post-processing if your model has bounds, and the approach works similarly in Gurobi as in CPLEX (perhaps up to a factor of -1).\n\n**Non-Uniqueness:**\nFarkas certificate is not unique, thus it is possible that two different software return different certificates; as long as both are valid, there is no reason to worry.\n\nThe search results contain discussions and examples from 2011-2023, but do not include specific 2024 developments on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4fc7aa2f-d0b8-4405-8f8e-896598f845d0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:54.930Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ce77d1b-f0fa-42fb-8c78-3caec27ab2c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8e46d1a8-f89b-4265-90d9-2b986a567e56","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SGhZhfq8Lrc1avMkuHX9t4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"anytime branch and bound epsilon bound carryover incumbent solver restart 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Branch and bound - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branch_and_bound\"},{\"title\":\"Spatial branch and bound method - Cornell University Computational Optimization Open Textbook - Optimization Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://optimization.cbe.cornell.edu/index.php?title=Spatial_branch_and_bound_method\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-Bound Algorithm Design - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/branch-and-bound-algorithm-design\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-Bound Algorithm - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/branch-and-bound-algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-Bound\",\"url\":\"https://www.hexaly.com/algorithms/branch-and-bound\"},{\"title\":\"Discrete Optimization with Branch and Bound - Matthew Crews\",\"url\":\"https://matthewcrews.com/blog/2018/2018-05-22-discrete-optimization-with-branch-and-bound/\"},{\"title\":\"The Branch-and-Bound Algorithm in Optimizing Mathematical Programming Models to Achieve Power Grid Observability\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2075-1680/12/11/1040\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-Bound for Integer Programming Problems\",\"url\":\"https://s2.smu.edu/~olinick/cse3360/lectures/b-and-b/l22.html\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-bound algorithms: A survey of recent advances in searching, branching, and pruning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528616000062\"},{\"title\":\"Branch and Bound Algorithm - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/branch-and-bound-algorithm/\"}]\n\nThe search results returned general information about branch-and-bound algorithms, epsilon-optimality, and incumbent solutions, but they don't contain specific research or papers from 2024 about \"anytime branch and bound\" with the specific combination of concepts you mentioned (epsilon bound carryover, incumbent solver restart).\n\nThe results discuss:\n- Branch-and-bound is a method for solving optimization problems by breaking them down into smaller subproblems and using a bounding function to eliminate subproblems that cannot contain the optimal solution\n- ε-globally optimal solutions where the optimum is bounded and the gap is less than ε\n- The incumbent solution is stored globally and updated at each iteration\n\nHowever, these general results don't appear to address the specific technical paper or research concept you're searching for related to anytime branch-and-bound with epsilon bound carryover and solver restart techniques from 2024. This appears to be a very specialized research topic that may require looking at academic databases, research preprint servers, or optimization conferences rather than general web search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"775942b8-559e-42f6-9f79-09d052468388","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:56.368Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e46d1a8-f89b-4265-90d9-2b986a567e56","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
