{"parentUuid":"254514f5-175f-437d-9f64-7d5d183c5af3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01V4HpctEGCkcMFScuvZuS8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KNfjuuDb1W2CuN2Gz1FYov","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"List parameters related to: hint, warm_start, cuts, cut_pool, share_objective, share_binary_clauses, restart, level_zero. Quote each parameter name and its 1-line meaning if visible."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10023,"cache_read_input_tokens":36024,"output_tokens":351,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10023},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":351,"cache_read_input_tokens":36024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caozh6MR1k7UARm6pTpHh","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e0af4fa7-d82c-4877-98ac-13dde9bfc293","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:03.823Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e0af4fa7-d82c-4877-98ac-13dde9bfc293","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNfjuuDb1W2CuN2Gz1FYov","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Parameters Related to Search Configuration\n\nBased on the proto file, here are the relevant parameters:\n\n**Hints & Warm Start:**\n- `use_optimization_hints`: \"For an optimization problem, whether we follow some hints in order to find a better first solution.\"\n\n**Objective Sharing:**\n- `share_objective_bounds`: \"Allows objective sharing between workers.\"\n\n**Clause Sharing:**\n- `share_binary_clauses`: \"Allows sharing of new learned binary clause between workers.\"\n- `share_glue_clauses`: \"Allows sharing of short glue clauses between workers.\"\n- `minimize_shared_clauses`: \"Minimize and detect subsumption of shared clauses immediately after they are imported.\"\n\n**Level Zero Bounds:**\n- `share_level_zero_bounds`: \"Allows sharing of the bounds of modified variables at level 0.\"\n\n**Restart Strategies:**\n- `restart_algorithms`: Configurable restart algorithm selection (LUBY, moving average variants, fixed)\n- `restart_period`: \"Restart period for the FIXED_RESTART strategy.\"\n- `restart_running_window_size`: \"Size of the window for the moving average restarts.\"\n\n**Additional Related:**\n- `num_conflicts_before_strategy_changes`: Triggers strategy switching after specified conflict count"}]},"uuid":"852023dc-4ada-4e94-ba15-46a5df5627ec","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:08.056Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e0af4fa7-d82c-4877-98ac-13dde9bfc293","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"254514f5-175f-437d-9f64-7d5d183c5af3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YHqjEwATnqYCPTZ5CAUcKU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"no-good cut\" persistence cross-iteration MIP CP solver portfolio 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving LBBD Master Problems with Constraint Programming ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.32/LIPIcs.CP.2024.32.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"An Efficient Local Search Solver for Mixed Integer Programming Peng Lin # Ñ\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.19/LIPIcs.CP.2024.19.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2024 L2P-MIP: LEARNING TO PRESOLVE FOR\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=McfYbKnpT8\"},{\"title\":\"CPLEX for MPL\",\"url\":\"https://www.maximalsoftware.com/solvers/cplex.html\"},{\"title\":\"Nogood Learning for Mixed Integer Programming Tuomas Sandholm Rob Shields\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~sandholm/nogoodsForMip.techReport06.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Rejecting MIP Solutions without lazy cuts – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360044353952-Rejecting-MIP-Solutions-without-lazy-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"MIP solver choice 2023 · google/or-tools · Discussion #3969\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3969\"},{\"title\":\"gams/cplex\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/49/docs/S_CPLEX.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/mip\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about no-good cuts and solver techniques from 2024:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe search returned academic papers from CP 2024 (Constraint Programming conference) that discuss cutting planes, constraint programming, and mixed integer programming solvers. Here's what I found:\n\n**No-good Learning and Cutting Planes:**\nA propagation-based nogood learning method for mixed integer programming (MIP) has been developed as an approach to improve solver performance. Modern complete propositional satisfiability solvers use nogood learning; it enables them to solve orders of magnitude larger problems.\n\n**Portfolio Solvers in 2024:**\nCP-SAT is a versatile portfolio solver, centered around a Lazy Clause Generation (LCG) based Constraint Programming Solver, and in its role as a portfolio solver, CP-SAT concurrently executes a multitude of diverse algorithms and strategies.\n\n**CP and MIP Integration (2024):**\nAs a constraint-based formalism, CP can readily accept cuts encoded as linear constraints, but linear constraints tend to propagate weakly, resulting in poor master problem performance, so more combinatorial encoding methods can focus on key decision variables in the global constraints of the master problem CP model.\n\nThe 2024 research indicates ongoing work on improving solver performance through better cut generation, nogood learning, and hybrid portfolio approaches that combine CP and MIP techniques across solver iterations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7c7ff610-a022-4b00-a520-c6f308901263","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:08.145Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"254514f5-175f-437d-9f64-7d5d183c5af3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a7987a4a-1acf-487b-b161-b10e159a8aab","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a823b529b0879c4bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R1JuCSufTHgthxejoHfkRr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" \"load_response\" OR \"SolverHint\" OR \"MPSolutionResponse\" warm restart between solves\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Restart CP-SAT from the current state in the solution process\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/5yh9MDP9neU\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Reuse variables in CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/UtMOv318dj4\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"warm start cp-sat ortools\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minizinc/c/1QRwbQhStHg\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT warm restart between solves:\n\nWarm-starting is an optimization where the solver uses the previous solution as a starting point or \"hint\" for the next iteration, which can significantly speed up the solving process, as the solver can often use the previous solution as a good starting point for repair, even if the previous solution becomes infeasible due to a newly added constraint.\n\nBecause repairing an infeasible hint can be computationally expensive, CP-SAT handles this process carefully, and you can instruct CP-SAT to attempt repairing the hint by setting solver.parameters.repair_hint = True.\n\nHowever, it's important to note that Solve is stateless, meaning CP-SAT's solve method does not retain state between calls, and while the input to CP-SAT is a CpModel proto that can be modified in place between solves, the gain will be minimal since the solver will still rescan the whole proto and restart from scratch each time.\n\nAdditionally, for advanced users working with CP-SAT incrementally (modifying and solving the model multiple times), the parameter fill_tightened_domains_in_response can be used to return tightened domains for variables, which can significantly reduce the search space and improve solver performance.\n\nCP-SAT prefers full hints, meaning all variables should be provided when warm-starting.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6a0f8dc9-97a1-414a-b244-a0d9dcadcaa1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:27:10.542Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a7987a4a-1acf-487b-b161-b10e159a8aab","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
